- For the remaining text, it computes a length (adjusting for HTML entities) and writes out either an 8BIM metadata block or an IPTC-style block to the output file, handling padding and reserved-length patches.
- It updates `outputlen` to track the number of bytes written and uses `savedpos`/`savedolen` pairs to back-patch lengths for IPTC records.
- At the end, it cleans up the tokenizer and any remaining buffers, and if needed back-patches a final length before returning the total bytes written.

