  return(-1);
```
If any of those checks fail, the function returns early without freeing the per-iteration buffers (`token`, `newstr`, `name`) nor the persistent buffer (`line`) or the tokenizer (`token_info`). Those allocations remain outstanding, resulting in a leak of heap memory when an I/O error occurs during blob positioning.

3. Decision

Yes, the code can leak memory on those early error returns because allocated buffers are not released before returning.

