1. Functional Analysis  
   - Retrieve the “class” object associated with the private script by name:  
     ```cpp
     v8::Local<v8::Object> classObject =
         classObjectOfPrivateScript(scriptState, className);
     ```  
   - Look up the property named `methodName` on that object and verify it’s a function. If not, log an error and abort:
     ```cpp
     if (!classObject->Get(..., v8String(..., methodName))
             .ToLocal(&method)
         || !method->IsFunction()) {
       fprintf(stderr, "Private script error: Target DOM method was not found. ...");
       RELEASE_NOTREACHED();
     }
     ```  
   - Ensure the provided `holder` object is correctly initialized for this class:
     ```cpp
     initializeHolderIfNeeded(scriptState, classObject, holder);
     ```  
   - Set up a V8 exception catcher on the isolate:
     ```cpp
     v8::TryCatch block(scriptState->isolate());
     ```  
   - Invoke the DOM method as an internal function call, passing in the `holder`, argument count, and argument array. If the call throws a JS exception:  
     a. Translate and rethrow it into the user-script context  
     b. Re-raise it on the original isolate  
     c. Return an empty handle  
     ```cpp
     if (!V8ScriptRunner::callInternalFunction(...)
             .ToLocal(&result)) {
